@define agent_roster():
### Confirmed agent roster

Model tiers are for reference only.

| agentType | Model tier | Role |
|-----------|-----------|------|
| Code | sonnet | Implements the plan and fixes review findings |
| Fix | sonnet | Fixes the listed validation, alignment and QA failures |
| Validate | haiku | Build / typecheck / lint / test — fast correctness gate |
| Polish | sonnet | Reduces complexity, removes duplication, improves readability |
| Harden | opus | 9-pillar self-review — deep structural analysis |
| Evaluate | sonnet | Plan-fidelity / alignment — "was the plan implemented correctly?" |
| Test | sonnet | Scenario-based acceptance tests against acceptance criteria |
| Review | opus | Focus-parameterized code review |
| Git | haiku | Git operations — branches, commits, merges, worktree management |
| Synthesize | haiku | Summarizes and aggregates multi-agent outputs |
| Knowledge | sonnet | Codebase exploration — feature knowledge base creation/update |
| Design | opus | Architecture and design — plans, gap analysis, design review |
@end

@define agent_caveats():
### Agent caveats

- **The Code family writes every fix** — Code for review findings, Fix for gate failures; no other agent type writes code. Finding verification uses adversarial Review passes.
- **Review agents are focus-parameterized.** Make one `agent()` call with `agentType: "Review"` per focus, with the focus in the prompt. Never batch focuses into one Review call.
- Give each agent its full context in its prompt.
@end

@export agent_roster
@export agent_caveats
